very day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple.<br><br>Present Continuous Tense <br><br>You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"italic\">to be + verb-ing</span>.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:<br><span class=\"bullet\">a current event or action happening around now  </span> <br><span class=\"bullet\">events that are going to happen soon (future plans)  </span> <br><br>You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We provide bus transportation from Waterloo Station.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm thinking about going to Stonehenge.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We take you to the Roman town of Bath.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Where are you staying?</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Great Britain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the country formed by England, Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Welcome to British Discoveries \u2026 the place to discover Great Britain!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le08ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you go on an excursion to Stonehenge.", "type": "tex